{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "e91AY25mSired-6rr",
			"description": "Splinter Pistol",
			"local_notes": "The shard is a small crystal sliver, so its wound multiplier is pi- (x1/2); the toxin follow-up is what kills. Line 2 is rolled only if line 1 penetrates DR (B414 follow-up rule).\n\nLore: The Kabalite sidearm: a slim crystal-shard projector loaded with a cartridge of toxin-tipped splinters. Codex: Drukhari background shows it carried by Kabalite Warriors, Sybarites and Wyches as the common Drukhari pistol; the pistol range is short and it trades reach for volume of poison rather than for punch.\n\nDesign: Scaled from the splinter rifle anchor (4d(3) pi-, 3d tox follow-up) by the framework's own pistol line, 3d(3) pi- + 2d tox, and not by shrinking the rifle: a smaller shard reservoir and shorter barrel put less velocity behind each sliver, and the cut in poison reflects a smaller dose per shard. Exact dice: 3d(3) averages 10.5 and penetrates flak (DR 30, effective 10) 50.0% of hits, carapace (DR 70, effective 23.3) 0.0% (1.7% counting the Weak Points chance), Astartes plate and Terminator plate 0.0%. A hit that gets through flak adds 2d tox (average 7) on top of about 1-3 injury from the shard: a wounded Guardsman-grade target drops in one or two hits. Handling: 2.5 lb loaded, so min ST 5 (sqrt(10x2.5)=5.0). RoF 3: a semi-automatic shard launcher fired as fast as the trigger allows (framework: 3 for semi-autos), a step under the rifle's 5. Shots 20(3): a small cartridge, quick to slap in. Acc 2 and Bulk -2 are ordinary pistol figures; Rcl 1 because a shard launcher has almost no kick. Range 50/200 keeps the rifle's 1:4 half/max shape at a third of the reach.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal"
			],
