		{
			"id": "egkoXTDB8SYN4TOq5",
			"description": "Splinter Rifle",
			"local_notes": "The shard is a small crystal sliver, so its wound multiplier is pi- (x1/2); the toxin follow-up is what kills. Line 2 is rolled only if line 1 penetrates DR (B414 follow-up rule).\n\nLore: The standard weapon of every Kabalite Warrior: a long, slender, faintly vicious rifle firing a stream of poison-coated crystal shards. Codex: Drukhari and older Codex: Dark Eldar background agree that its power lies in the toxin, which is why it is fielded in numbers against foes it could never hurt by kinetic force alone; the shards themselves are light and do little damage to armoured targets.\n\nDesign: This is the framework's fixed anchor: 4d(3) pi- with a 3d tox follow-up, RoF about 5, range about 150/600 (the framework's 'about' is kept: Acc, weight and handling are derived here). Exact dice: 4d(3) averages 14; it penetrates flak (effective 10) 84.1% of hits (86.7% with the Weak Points chance for flak WP 7), carapace (effective 23.3) 0.1% (3.6% with WP 5), Astartes plate (effective 33.3) 0.0% (0.4% with WP 4) and Terminator plate 0.0%: exactly 'stopped by carapace except on a Weak Point'. Against an unarmoured or flak-armoured man the shard's pi- injury is small but the 3d tox follow-up (average 10.5) is not: one penetrating hit averages about 12-17 injury, more than a Guardsman's 10 HP. A lasgun hit (7d(2) burn) is the comparison: the splinter rifle is a poorer weapon against armour and a better one against flesh. Handling: 6 lb loaded (a lasgun is 8 lb; this is a light, elegant Aeldari-style frame), min ST 8 (sqrt(60)=7.7). RoF 5 is the anchor. Acc 5 for a rifle-length barrel with a good sight radius; Bulk -5 for its length; Rcl 1 because the shard launcher barely kicks (framework: beams 1, pistols 2-3, rifles 2-3, so this is deliberately at the beam end). Shots 60(3): a shard cartridge, an honest design number since the sources give no capacity.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
