		{
			"id": "eFJ94r4zjWgh6vi9e",
			"description": "Shardcarbine",
			"local_notes": "The shard is a small crystal sliver, so its wound multiplier is pi- (x1/2); the toxin follow-up is what kills. Line 2 is rolled only if line 1 penetrates DR (B414 follow-up rule).\n\nLore: A short, fast-firing splinter weapon used by Kabalite Warriors, Sybarites and by winged Scourges who want a compact weapon in the air; Codex: Drukhari background describes the Scourge as carrying it, and it is the same weapon in the hands of either. It is a rapid-fire carbine version of the splinter rifle: shorter reach, greater volume.\n\nDesign: The framework anchor says 'rifle damage, higher RoF, shorter range', so the dice are unchanged from the splinter rifle (4d(3) pi- + 3d tox; every penetration figure there applies: 84.1% flak, 0.1% carapace, 0.0% Astartes) and the handling is re-derived. Range 75/300 is half the rifle's, the usual carbine trade. RoF 12 (up from 5, within the framework's 10-12 for automatic rifles) reflects a faster shard cycle. Weight 4.5 lb, min ST 7 (sqrt(45)=6.7). Acc 3 (framework: carbines 3-4) and Bulk -3 (carbines); Rcl 1 as for all splinter weapons. Shots 90(3): a larger cartridge to feed the higher rate (7 seconds of fire). The Scourge shardcarbine is not a separate weapon here: background gives it the same role and no distinct profile, so it uses this entry.",
