		{
			"id": "eCZyEH1nbHhYxZ1gt",
			"description": "Splinter Cannon",
			"local_notes": "The shard is a small crystal sliver, so its wound multiplier is pi- (x1/2); the toxin follow-up is what kills. Line 2 is rolled only if line 1 penetrates DR (B414 follow-up rule).\n\nLore: The Kabal's heavy support weapon, carried by Kabalite Trueborn and fitted to Raiders, Ravagers and other Kabal vehicles; a large-bore splinter launcher that sprays poisoned crystal at a rate a rifle cannot match (Codex: Drukhari and older Codex: Dark Eldar). It is more feared for its volume than for the strength of any single shard.\n\nDesign: The framework anchor is 5d(3) pi- + 3d tox with RoF 15+; RoF 16 is chosen (anchor 'RoF 15+'). Exact dice: 5d(3) averages 17.5, penetrating flak (effective 10) 96.8%, carapace (effective 23.3) 5.9% (10.0% with WP 5), Astartes plate 0.0% (1.1% with WP 4) and Terminator plate 0.0%: a real if unreliable carapace-breaker, still no threat to power armour. The 3d tox follow-up is the same as a rifle's, so a cannon burst is about the rate of fire, not a stronger poison. Handling: 22 lb loaded (a light-weight support weapon by human standards), so min ST sqrt(10x22)=14.8, 15, with a bipod (B): a Kabalite Warrior at ST 10 must brace it or fire at a penalty, as a Guardsman does with a heavy weapon. Acc 5 (a heavier, steadier barrel than a rifle's), Bulk -6 (support weapon), Rcl 2 (volume of shards rather than mass). Shots 200(5): a large feed drum. Range 175/700, a modest step up from the rifle's 150/600 for the longer barrel. Skill Guns (Light Machine Gun), as for the Aeldari shuriken cannon.",
