		{
			"id": "eljFoAyWkJhQbAJ6g",
			"description": "Blast Pistol",
			"local_notes": "Armour divisor (10): the beam drills a narrow hole through any armour to the same depth.\n\nLore: A hand-held dark-lance weapon carried by Archons, Sybarites and Hekatrixes who want a beam of anti-armour power at pistol reach (Codex: Drukhari background). It fires a narrow, focused burst and needs a moment to recover between shots; nothing in the sources gives it long range.\n\nDesign: Anchored by the framework: 6dx2(10) burn, short range, the hand-weapon step below the blaster's 6dx3 and the dark lance's 6dx4 (same focused-beam technology at 1/2, 3/4 and full 4x multiplier of a 6d core). Exact dice: 6dx2 averages 42; the divisor (10) makes effective DR 3 (flak), 7 (carapace), 10 (Astartes) and 19 (Terminator), so it penetrates flak, carapace and Astartes plate 100.0% of hits and Terminator plate 99.8%. This is the bright-lance logic at pistol scale: the divisor, not the dice, does the work, and the weapon is held back by short range (20/60) and a tiny charge rather than by damage. Vehicles: AV10 100%, AV12 99.5%, AV13 96.4%, AV14 79.4%. Handling: 3.5 lb loaded, min ST 6 (sqrt(35)=5.9). RoF 1 because the beam capacitor must recover between shots (framework: RoF 1 for anything that must recharge). Shots 3(4): a small charge cell, a shot fewer than the Aeldari fusion pistol's, since a dark-lance beam is a bigger draw per shot. Acc 2 (framework: pistols 1-3), Bulk -2, Rcl 1 (beam).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal"
			],
			"tech_level": "11^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "3500",
			"base_weight": "3.5 lb",
			"weapons": [
