		{
			"id": "e1x0KnVuMhDYqBit2",
			"description": "Dark Lance",
			"local_notes": "Armour divisor (10). The B in Min ST means bipod-braced.\n\nLore: The Drukhari answer to the Aeldari bright lance: a heavy anti-armour weapon carried by Kabalite Trueborn and fitted to Raiders and Ravagers, and one of the most feared weapons in a Kabal's arsenal against vehicles and heavy infantry (Codex: Drukhari background). The Drukhari version is a darker, more brutal cousin of the craftworld weapon.\n\nDesign: The framework anchor: 'as the bright lance: 6dx4(10) burn'. The dice are kept exactly (6dx4(10), average 84) with the same argument as the bright lance: the focused beam penetrates all armour to the same depth, so effective DR never exceeds 35 and it penetrates flak, carapace, Astartes plate and Terminator plate 100.0% of hits, and vehicles AV10-14 at 100.0/100.0/100.0/100.0/99.9%. Handling is re-derived rather than copied: 26 lb loaded (the Aeldari bright lance is 28 lb; this is a rougher build), so min ST sqrt(260)=16.1, 16, with a bipod (16B), in line with the framework's shoulder-weapon rule; the Kabalite ST 10 fires it at a heavy penalty unless braced, so it is normally mounted or fired prone. Acc 8 (a vehicle-style optic on a shoulder weapon, less than the bright lance's 9 for the cruder sight), range 1000/3000 (slightly under the bright lance's 1200/3600), RoF 1 (recharge), Shots 4(6) (fewer than the bright lance's 6, a heavy draw per shot), Bulk -7, Rcl 1.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal"
			],
			"tech_level": "11^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "12000",
			"base_weight": "26 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "Wd8wvAZmmP235eghq",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "burn",
						"base": "6dx4",
						"armor_divisor": 10
					},
					"accuracy": "8",
					"range": "1000/3000",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "4(6)",
					"bulk": "-7",
					"recoil": "1",
					"strength": "16B",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -4
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
