		{
			"id": "etxvV85UWO2GsD9gn",
			"description": "Disintegrator Cannon",
			"local_notes": "Does not overheat: no Malf on any roll. The 'ex' marks an explosive burn: a hit is a detonation, so damage is rolled as for explosions, not as a beam.\n\nLore: A heavy Drukhari energy weapon carried by Trueborn and fitted to Raiders, Ravagers and Razorwings: a rapid discharge of unstable energy that, in Codex: Drukhari background, is known for stripping armour and flesh alike. Unlike an Imperial plasma gun it does not overheat.\n\nDesign: The framework anchor is 'plasma class like the starcannon, no overheating'. It is the Aeldari starcannon's dice with one die removed: 5dx4(3) burn ex against the starcannon's 6dx4(3), because the sources put the Drukhari weapon a small step below the Aeldari one (background gives only the ordering, never a number, so the exact step is a design call). Exact dice: average 70; effective DR under divisor (3) is 10 (flak), 23.3 (carapace), 33.3 (Astartes) and 63.3 (Terminator): it penetrates flak and carapace 100.0%, Astartes plate 99.3% and Terminator plate 69.5% (more often than not, as a plasma weapon should). Vehicles AV10-14: 99.3/90.2/60.0/9.8/0.0%: it kills light and medium vehicles but not a Land Raider. RoF 4 (the starcannon is 3): with no vent cycle to wait on, the limit is the charge chamber's refresh. Weight 20 lb, min ST sqrt(200)=14.1, 14, with a bipod (14B). Acc 5, range 200/600, Shots 12(4), Bulk -6, Rcl 2 (a weighty discharge).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal"
			],
			"tech_level": "11^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "8000",
			"base_weight": "20 lb",
			"weapons": [
