		{
			"id": "e_UMGJAyaWs-nA_S1",
			"description": "Haywire Blaster",
			"local_notes": "Powered armour, cyborgs and vehicle machine-spirits are machines for these purposes (GM's call for sealed power armour: a wearer's servos and vox may fail rather than his body).\n\nLore: An electromagnetic pulse projector used by Drukhari raiders to take down vehicles and cybernetics, carried by Kabalite Trueborn and fitted to Raiders (Codex: Drukhari background). It leaves flesh almost unharmed and turns armour to scrap.\n\nDesign: The framework says 'anti-machine pulse: big damage to vehicles and electronics, near nothing to flesh'. Following the Adeptus Mechanicus arc weapons in this project (weak against flesh, strong against machines), it has two lines. Against flesh it is a nuisance: 1d burn, which penetrates nothing (flak effective DR 30, 0.0%). Against machines the 4dx3 (average 42) ignores DR because the pulse is delivered through a vehicle's plating into its systems, so armour thickness matters not at all; the HT-4 disable is the Arc Rifle's surge mechanic scaled to the weapon's larger discharge. It is not a hull-buster: 42 average against a vehicle's structural HP is meaningful, not decisive, and the weapon is really a systems-killer. Handling: 10 lb loaded, min ST 10 (sqrt(100)=10). RoF 1 (capacitor recharge). Acc 4, range 100/300 (lower than an ordinary rifle, a pulse projector), Shots 5(4), Bulk -5, Rcl 1.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Kabal"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "4000",
			"base_weight": "10 lb",
			"weapons": [
