		{
			"id": "eCVWOj8e9_ci_Q0wZ",
			"description": "Hexrifle",
			"local_notes": "A sniper toxin weapon: aimed shots with the Accuracy bonus for Aim.\n\nLore: A long-barrelled sniper weapon used by poisoners and marksmen, firing a shard loaded with a toxin said to bring down anything from a man to a monster (Codex: Drukhari background). It does not kill by armour penetration but by poison. Background places it with the Kabals and Covens; I am not certain which arsenal lists it, so it carries both tags.\n\nDesign: The framework says 'sniper toxin that no armour stops once a shard lands'. That is modelled directly: line 2 is a 5d tox (average 17.5) follow-up that applies whenever the shot hits, with no DR check. This deliberately breaks the follow-up rule the splinter weapons use (only if the shard penetrates), because the hexrifle is the exception the sources describe. The shard itself is a needle (3d(3) pi-, the splinter pistol's dice: penetrates flak 50.0%, carapace 0.0%). 5d is chosen so that roughly two hits bring down a Space Marine (HP 34, average two hits 35) but one leaves him standing; against an unarmoured man (HP 10) one hit is enough. Handling: 7 lb (a long, slim rifle), min ST 8 (sqrt(70)=8.4). Acc 8 (framework: rifle 5, optics +1 to +3, +3 here). RoF 1 (bolt-action style aimed shot), Shots 10(3), range 250/1000 (well beyond the splinter rifle's 150/600). Bulk -6, Rcl 1.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
