		{
			"id": "ezOM56USsP1pSND-I",
			"description": "Liquifier Gun",
			"local_notes": "Corrosion (cor) wounds x1 as burn does. Sealed armour delays the follow-up; see that line.\n\nLore: A close-range weapon of the Haemonculus Coven that sprays a gel or liquid which dissolves the target's flesh (Codex: Drukhari background). Wracks carry it, and it is best at packing a squad into a corridor. Background gives no more than that.\n\nDesign: No framework number beyond 'close-range dissolving flamer'. Built from the flamer design: a 5-yard cone (B281), a hit-then-follow-up structure where the first roll is small and the real killing is the damage that keeps coming. The first hit is 3d cor (average 10.5, 0.0% against flak; it does not reach armour); the gel then dissolves, 2d cor per turn ignoring DR for 1d turns, which is what makes it feared. Where the Imperial flamer's follow-up does not affect sealed armour at all, the gel eats through seals, so sealed armour gets only a one-turn delay. Handling: 11 lb, min ST 10 (sqrt(110)=10.5); shots 6(4) is a small tank. RoF 1 and Bulk -4; Acc and Rcl are omitted for a cone weapon.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Drukhari",
				"Haemonculus Coven"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "3000",
			"base_weight": "11 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WqiaQP8vN8xISG590",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cor",
						"base": "3d"
					},
					"range": "5",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "6(4)",
					"bulk": "-4",
					"strength": "10",
					"usage": "Cone (5 yards)",
					"usage_notes": "As the flamer: no Acc, no aiming roll inside the cone; each target rolled separately.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -4
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
